WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:01.149
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:01.982
It's Evan.

00:00:01.982 --> 00:00:03.471
My one word is believe,

00:00:03.471 --> 00:00:04.732
and I believe in people

00:00:04.732 --> 00:00:06.377
more than they believe in themselves,

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:09.059
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:10.390
what I see in you,

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.360
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.486
So to help you on your journey.

00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:16.356
Today's message is paint what you want.

00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:18.051
Over to you, Warren Buffet.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.224
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:21.057
(hip-hop music)

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:23.259
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:25.910
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.053
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:32.673
- What brings you the most satisfaction?

00:00:32.673 --> 00:00:34.184
Beyond family.

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:37.558
- Well, (laughs) my most
greatest satisfaction

00:00:37.558 --> 00:00:39.399
is just staying in good health.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:40.973
I mean, when you're 86, I mean,

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.524
you look at this a little differently.

00:00:42.524 --> 00:00:44.121
(laughter)

00:00:44.121 --> 00:00:44.954
But I...

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:45.991
- So you're in good health?

00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:46.824
- Oh yeah.

00:00:46.824 --> 00:00:49.113
I mean, I enjoy every day, I enjoy...

00:00:49.113 --> 00:00:50.737
- [Interviewer] But what
is it that you enjoy?

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:52.820
- Well, I enjoy running Berkshire.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.492
I mean, if you get right down
into my psyche, I mean...

00:00:55.492 --> 00:00:56.328
- [Interviewer] That's
what I want to hear.

00:00:56.328 --> 00:00:57.806
- Yeah, no, it's, you know,

00:00:57.806 --> 00:01:00.645
it's been my painting for 50-some years.

00:01:00.645 --> 00:01:01.893
I get to paint what I want.

00:01:01.893 --> 00:01:03.765
I don't have to do, you know,

00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:07.648
follow what Wall Street is
telling me to do next quarter

00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:08.588
or something like that.

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:11.092
So I own the brush, I own the canvas,

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:12.719
and the canvas is unlimited,

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:14.320
and that's a pretty nice game,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.039
and I get to do it every
day with people I like.

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:20.035
I don't have to associate with anyone

00:01:20.035 --> 00:01:22.282
that causes my stomach to churn, you know?

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.445
If I were in politics,

00:01:23.445 --> 00:01:25.153
I'd have to smile at a lot of people

00:01:25.153 --> 00:01:26.937
that I want to hit, you know?

00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:27.770
- So...

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.804
- [Interviewer] You
just don't talk to them.

00:01:28.804 --> 00:01:29.637
- So I...

00:01:29.637 --> 00:01:31.079
It's really, I've got a good deal.

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:33.023
I'm going to, I'm hanging onto it.

00:01:33.023 --> 00:01:34.012
(laughter)

00:01:34.012 --> 00:01:35.372
- This is always a great reminder

00:01:35.372 --> 00:01:38.209
that you are in control of your own brush.

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:40.261
You are the artist, you
get to paint what you want,

00:01:40.261 --> 00:01:42.170
and you are in control of your brush.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.311
Where too often we blame other people.

00:01:44.311 --> 00:01:45.355
You might blame your boss

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:46.991
if you have a job that
you're trying to get out of.

00:01:46.991 --> 00:01:48.478
You might blame your circumstances.

00:01:48.478 --> 00:01:50.556
And as soon as you start
blaming somebody else,

00:01:50.556 --> 00:01:52.491
it makes you feel good about yourself,

00:01:52.491 --> 00:01:54.345
'cuz it's not your fault anymore, right?

00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:55.880
So it's somebody else's fault,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.277
so I can feel better about myself.

00:01:57.277 --> 00:02:00.263
But as soon as you give
away that responsibility,

00:02:00.263 --> 00:02:03.956
as soon as you give your
brush to somebody else,

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.323
then you're never going to grow.

00:02:05.323 --> 00:02:06.187
It's hopeless.

00:02:06.187 --> 00:02:08.229
You're never going to make
the painting that you want.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:11.153
And so it always starts with
you picking up your brush

00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:13.070
and owning your canvas,

00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:15.535
and that may not be a full-time thing.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.443
Like, there's the realities of the world.

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:19.189
You might have a family,
you might have kids,

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:20.970
you might have a spouse,
you might have big debt.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.572
There's lots of reasons, you know,

00:02:22.572 --> 00:02:24.798
that are slowing your progress,

00:02:24.798 --> 00:02:27.329
but you can still pick
up that brush every day

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:28.897
and paint something, right?

00:02:28.897 --> 00:02:31.343
You can spend 30 to 60
minutes every single day

00:02:31.343 --> 00:02:32.341
on your business,

00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:33.378
and if you did that,

00:02:33.378 --> 00:02:36.437
you'll start to see major
growth in your business.

00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:39.407
What ends up happening
is the pressures of life

00:02:39.407 --> 00:02:41.269
and everything else that's happening

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:42.515
start beating down on you.

00:02:42.515 --> 00:02:43.955
You haven't scheduled in enough time

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:45.344
to focus on your business.

00:02:45.344 --> 00:02:47.275
You don't set enough boundaries around it

00:02:47.275 --> 00:02:49.353
and say this is sacred
time that I need to focus

00:02:49.353 --> 00:02:51.791
on doing the thing that I
say I want to do, right?

00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:52.941
If you have this big goal,

00:02:52.941 --> 00:02:55.687
you have to start matching
your actions to the goal.

00:02:55.687 --> 00:02:56.520
You start out,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.154
you have to start taking
action on the thing

00:02:58.154 --> 00:02:59.331
that you say you want to do.

00:02:59.331 --> 00:03:00.659
You have to pick up your brush

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:03.259
and every day start painting.

00:03:03.259 --> 00:03:04.790
And so for those of you
who haven't gone full-time

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.668
or aren't taking enough action,

00:03:06.668 --> 00:03:10.044
schedule in the time in
your calendar consistently

00:03:10.044 --> 00:03:12.041
so that it's happening.

00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:14.573
So, you know, Monday nights at 9:00

00:03:14.573 --> 00:03:16.445
and Tuesday nights at 9:00

00:03:16.445 --> 00:03:19.263
or whatever the time is that
fits best for your schedule,

00:03:19.263 --> 00:03:22.790
make sure it's being put in
there so you have time to paint.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.376
The other side are the entrepreneurs
who start to get bored.

00:03:25.376 --> 00:03:28.215
The entrepreneurs who have a business,

00:03:28.215 --> 00:03:29.075
who've had some success,

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.145
but then they've plateaued,

00:03:30.145 --> 00:03:32.223
and they're kind of just
staying here at the same level,

00:03:32.223 --> 00:03:34.378
not growing, not getting
anything from it anymore.

00:03:34.378 --> 00:03:35.923
And a lot of these
entrepreneurs, this is common.

00:03:35.923 --> 00:03:37.623
It's common to get bored of your business.

00:03:37.623 --> 00:03:40.613
It's common to then want
to quit your business,

00:03:40.613 --> 00:03:42.968
or to look for something
else that you want to do

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.521
because this business isn't giving you

00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:46.629
the satisfaction and the joy anymore.

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:48.135
And a big reason for that

00:03:48.135 --> 00:03:50.166
is because you've dropped the brush.

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:52.136
Like, you've stopped
creating something new.

00:03:52.136 --> 00:03:53.552
You let the success that
you've had in the past

00:03:53.552 --> 00:03:56.217
be chains that prevent
you from moving forward.

00:03:56.217 --> 00:03:57.239
So I was talking to a YouTuber recently

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.197
who's going through this,

00:03:58.197 --> 00:04:00.146
and he has a successful channel,

00:04:00.146 --> 00:04:01.244
he's trying to build it up,

00:04:01.244 --> 00:04:02.830
but he's had kind of flat growth,

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.357
and he feels like he's
making the same videos

00:04:04.357 --> 00:04:06.026
over and over and over again,

00:04:06.026 --> 00:04:08.073
and there's no variety
in the content anymore,

00:04:08.073 --> 00:04:09.575
and he's not sure what to do about it.

00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:10.655
Should he sell his channel?

00:04:10.655 --> 00:04:12.303
Should he focus on a different business?

00:04:12.303 --> 00:04:13.905
Should he set up other joint ventures?

00:04:13.905 --> 00:04:15.102
Should he get into podcasting?

00:04:15.102 --> 00:04:17.047
Should he just go and do something else?

00:04:17.047 --> 00:04:18.907
And the reason why he's
frustrated and bored

00:04:18.907 --> 00:04:20.914
is because he lost the creativity.

00:04:20.914 --> 00:04:22.595
He's not doing new things anymore, right?

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.466
He dropped his brush.

00:04:24.466 --> 00:04:25.736
You have to pick it back up

00:04:25.736 --> 00:04:28.004
and just start to paint again
and do something different.

00:04:28.004 --> 00:04:29.921
I love the series on my channel.

00:04:29.921 --> 00:04:31.684
I love making every new series.

00:04:31.684 --> 00:04:34.691
I'm constantly inviting new series in.

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.606
If I don't like a series
anymore, I'll drop it,

00:04:36.606 --> 00:04:37.659
even if it's really popular,

00:04:37.659 --> 00:04:39.668
if I'm not enjoying it,
I'm going to drop it,

00:04:39.668 --> 00:04:42.745
because I don't want to come
here and talk to you guys

00:04:42.745 --> 00:04:45.813
on a consistent basis on something
I'm not passionate about.

00:04:45.813 --> 00:04:47.099
And so we're constantly trying new things,

00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:48.611
new series, new ideas.

00:04:48.611 --> 00:04:49.780
I'm constantly painting.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.610
My channel is not the same.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.586
Yes, we're making YouTube videos,

00:04:53.586 --> 00:04:55.475
but it's not the same as I was a year ago,

00:04:55.475 --> 00:04:57.067
and it's not going to
look the same as it will

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.472
in another year from now,

00:04:58.472 --> 00:05:00.299
and two years, and five
years, and 10 years.

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:02.044
And so the key is to
be constantly evolving

00:05:02.044 --> 00:05:03.429
as an entrepreneur,

00:05:03.429 --> 00:05:04.844
constantly picking up the brush,

00:05:04.844 --> 00:05:06.452
constantly painting new things,

00:05:06.452 --> 00:05:09.252
and if you go too long as
a creative entrepreneur

00:05:09.252 --> 00:05:11.647
without painting, without expressing,

00:05:11.647 --> 00:05:13.572
without putting yourself
into the business,

00:05:13.572 --> 00:05:15.233
and you just get stuck
in the day to day grind

00:05:15.233 --> 00:05:16.999
of running the operations,

00:05:16.999 --> 00:05:19.827
you will get bored, you will crash,

00:05:19.827 --> 00:05:21.318
you will want to shut down,

00:05:21.318 --> 00:05:22.660
you will want to look at something else,

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.956
you will want to sell the business,

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.693
you will want to move on.

00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:26.802
And so if that's you,

00:05:26.802 --> 00:05:28.454
I'd strongly encourage you to look at

00:05:28.454 --> 00:05:31.363
how do I consistently find new ways

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:35.323
to pick up the brush and
keep painting in my business.

00:05:35.323 --> 00:05:37.064
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:05:37.064 --> 00:05:39.927
how often are you creating
new things for your business?

00:05:39.927 --> 00:05:42.111
How often are you
expressing your creativity

00:05:42.111 --> 00:05:44.085
into your company?

00:05:44.085 --> 00:05:45.565
How consistent is that for you?

00:05:45.565 --> 00:05:46.398
Is it daily?

00:05:46.398 --> 00:05:47.283
Is it once a week?

00:05:47.283 --> 00:05:48.391
Is it once a month?

00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:49.324
Is it once a quarter?

00:05:49.324 --> 00:05:50.494
I'd love to hear from you.

00:05:50.494 --> 00:05:51.856
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:05:51.856 --> 00:05:53.321
Also, for people who leave comments

00:05:53.321 --> 00:05:55.740
within the first few hours
of this video going live,

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.314
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:05:58.314 --> 00:06:00.539
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Marcus Campbell.

00:06:00.539 --> 00:06:01.995
Marcus, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:01.995 --> 00:06:03.558
a copy of my book "Your One Word"

00:06:03.558 --> 00:06:05.827
and making the YouTube
video on it, as well.

00:06:05.827 --> 00:06:08.746
I really, really appreciate
the support and the review,

00:06:08.746 --> 00:06:10.752
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed my book.

00:06:10.752 --> 00:06:12.023
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:12.023 --> 00:06:13.062
I believe in you.

00:06:13.062 --> 00:06:14.902
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:14.902 --> 00:06:16.661
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:16.661 --> 00:06:17.683
Much love,

00:06:17.683 --> 00:06:19.275
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:19.275 --> 00:06:21.642
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:21.642 --> 00:06:22.475
(hip-hop music)

00:06:22.475 --> 00:06:24.245
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:24.245 --> 00:06:27.662
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:06:31.037 --> 00:06:35.120
- I think you've got to
find what makes you tick.

00:06:36.461 --> 00:06:40.628
And I think greatness comes
from when you marry your passion

00:06:42.424 --> 00:06:43.591
with your job.

00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:46.392
'Cuz I don't really think I have a job.

00:06:46.392 --> 00:06:47.991
I just, I love what I do.

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:49.289
And I always say that to kids.

00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:51.750
I talk to a lot of kids who
are at university and say,

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.101
how do I make a lot of money?

00:06:53.101 --> 00:06:54.765
I say, forget the lot of money part.

00:06:54.765 --> 00:06:56.735
Find something you're going to be great at

00:06:56.735 --> 00:06:58.627
and let the money follow you.

00:06:58.627 --> 00:07:01.861
- So what is it about people
who find their passion,

00:07:01.861 --> 00:07:03.798
who work hard and never make a dime?

00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:07.577
Well, they make a few
dimes, but not enough.

00:07:07.577 --> 00:07:08.761
They never get there.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.456
- So, you know, Fanny, it's interesting,

00:07:10.456 --> 00:07:13.598
'cuz we have this
conversation all the time.

00:07:13.598 --> 00:07:15.686
I live in a very affluent area,

00:07:15.686 --> 00:07:18.020
and I have these quarterly dinners,

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.544
or I used to, with my neighbors.

00:07:19.544 --> 00:07:22.074
So at one point I had 20 guys.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.906
They were all worth hundreds
of millions of dollars.

00:07:23.906 --> 00:07:25.730
And we asked that same question.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:28.618
Can you always be successful,

00:07:28.618 --> 00:07:30.864
even if you love what you
do and all the other stuff?

00:07:30.864 --> 00:07:33.658
And the reality is, as my dad said,

00:07:33.658 --> 00:07:35.040
- If you work hard...
- [Fanny] Right.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.364
- ...you will never be poor in life.

00:07:37.364 --> 00:07:41.242
But just because you work hard
doesn't mean you'll be rich.

00:07:41.242 --> 00:07:43.618
Sometimes you need to get lucky.

00:07:43.618 --> 00:07:46.326
But the reality is that
the harder you work,

00:07:46.326 --> 00:07:48.096
it's true, the luckier you get.

00:07:48.096 --> 00:07:50.058
- So I don't really remember
the exact day or anything,

00:07:50.058 --> 00:07:52.256
but when I was in college
is when I started thinking

00:07:52.256 --> 00:07:56.298
about wanting to be an
entrepreneur someday.

00:07:56.298 --> 00:08:00.015
So it was, I was not the
kid with the lemonade stand.

00:08:00.015 --> 00:08:00.848
You know, I didn't,

00:08:00.848 --> 00:08:01.946
I wasn't one of these kids

00:08:01.946 --> 00:08:03.369
who was always trying to raise money.

00:08:03.369 --> 00:08:04.952
I always wanted to be a
scientist when I was little.

00:08:04.952 --> 00:08:07.020
But I'd also always loved computers.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.495
I like, I was lucky, 'cuz
at my age this is unusual,

00:08:10.495 --> 00:08:12.540
to have access to a mainframe computer

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.060
for my elementary school
when I was in fourth grade,

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.498
and quickly learned that there was

00:08:17.498 --> 00:08:20.160
a pre-programmed Star Trek
game on that computer,

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.912
and then I never did anything
except play Star Trek

00:08:21.912 --> 00:08:22.795
with the computer.

00:08:22.795 --> 00:08:24.812
So I don't know how formative that was.

00:08:24.812 --> 00:08:25.645
It certainly led,

00:08:25.645 --> 00:08:27.970
it certainly helped my Star
Trek knowledge considerably.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:28.803
(laughter)

00:08:28.803 --> 00:08:31.588
And, and, but I've always loved computers.

00:08:31.588 --> 00:08:32.809
Somewhere in college,

00:08:32.809 --> 00:08:35.110
I started watching some of
the people who were, like,

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.069
setting up, you know, college
pizza delivery services,

00:08:39.069 --> 00:08:41.026
and, you know, kind of
the core entrepreneurs,

00:08:41.026 --> 00:08:42.066
and thinking, you know,

00:08:42.066 --> 00:08:44.632
this looks like a really fun thing to do.

00:08:44.632 --> 00:08:46.759
- I mean, I really,
really enjoy what I do.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.019
I really do.

00:08:48.019 --> 00:08:49.036
And I think, you know,

00:08:49.036 --> 00:08:51.985
a number of you probably are
interested in consulting,

00:08:51.985 --> 00:08:53.373
and I think my only advice,

00:08:53.373 --> 00:08:56.577
and I hope that I'm a
few years older than you

00:08:56.577 --> 00:08:58.951
so I have the right to give
you a little bit of advice.

00:08:58.951 --> 00:09:00.889
But my only advice is pick something

00:09:00.889 --> 00:09:03.009
that you will thoroughly enjoy,

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.547
whatever that may be.

00:09:04.547 --> 00:09:07.111
And I think if you do that, you know,

00:09:07.111 --> 00:09:09.624
you will, to answer the
first individual's question,

00:09:09.624 --> 00:09:11.233
you'll probably survive in it,

00:09:11.233 --> 00:09:14.239
and potentially, maybe
you'll thrive in it.

00:09:14.239 --> 00:09:15.435
I mean, I usually don't say this,

00:09:15.435 --> 00:09:20.053
but, you know, if I wasn't
paid a lot of money,

00:09:20.053 --> 00:09:23.071
I would still do what I do.

00:09:23.071 --> 00:09:24.661
I hope, you know,

00:09:24.661 --> 00:09:27.654
some of our managing partners
don't see this program,

00:09:27.654 --> 00:09:28.487
(laughter)

00:09:28.487 --> 00:09:29.813
because my units may get cut.

00:09:29.813 --> 00:09:32.396
But I would still do what I do.

00:09:33.926 --> 00:09:36.140
You know, I'm surprised on a yearly basis

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:38.477
as to what kind of money I make.

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:40.494
I mean, I just am absolutely surprised.

00:09:40.494 --> 00:09:44.112
I would do it for a tenth of what I make.

00:09:44.112 --> 00:09:46.649
So, you know, just find
something that you really enjoy,

00:09:46.649 --> 00:09:48.134
and I think you'll thrive.

